---
/**
 * Privacy notice for the early access list.
 *
 * DRAFT for Freddie to confirm. Items marked "to be confirmed" (data-tbc) must be
 * filled in before go-live: search this file for "data-tbc".
 * When the wording changes, update LAST_UPDATED.
 */
import SimplePage from '@/components/layout/SimplePage.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';

const LAST_UPDATED = { iso: '2026-10-30', label: '30 October 2026' };

// Visible but quiet marker for details still to be confirmed.
const tbc =
  'rounded-[3px] border border-dashed border-estuary/50 bg-sailcloth px-1.5 py-px text-[0.9em] font-normal whitespace-nowrap text-estuary';

const prose = [
  '[&_h2]:mt-14 [&_h2]:font-serif [&_h2]:text-title [&_h2]:text-driftwood',
  '[&_p]:mt-4 [&_ul]:mt-4 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_li]:mt-2 [&_li]:pl-1 [&_li]:marker:text-estuary',
  '[&_a]:underline [&_a]:decoration-driftwood/35 [&_a]:underline-offset-[0.2em] [&_a:hover]:decoration-driftwood',
  '[&_strong]:font-medium',
].join(' ');
---

<SimplePage
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How Sea Air Club looks after the details you give us when you join the early access list."
>
  <article class="px-(--gutter) pt-16 pb-(--section-y) md:pt-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[680px]">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow text-estuary">Early access list</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 font-serif text-heading">Privacy notice</h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-small text-driftwood/75">
          Last updated <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED.iso}>{LAST_UPDATED.label}</time>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-8 text-body-l">
          When you join the Sea Air Club early access list, you trust us with a few details. This
          notice explains, in plain terms, what we collect, why, where it's kept and the choices you
          have.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class={`text-body ${prose}`}>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <!-- prettier-ignore -->
        <p>
          Sea Air Club is run by <span class={tbc} data-tbc>[legal name to be confirmed]</span>,
          <span class={tbc} data-tbc>[registered address to be confirmed]</span>. We're the
          <strong>controller</strong> of the personal data described here, which means we decide how
          it's used and we're responsible for looking after it.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>When you join the early access list, we keep:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your email address</li>
          <li>your first name, if you choose to give it</li>
          <li>
            how you found us: the campaign tags in the link you followed (known as UTM tags, for
            example from a postcard, our QR code or Instagram) and the page you first landed on
          </li>
          <li>
            the date and time you joined, and which version of the sign-up wording you agreed to, so
            we have a record of your consent
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We don't save your IP address with your sign-up. Like most websites, our hosting provider
          keeps short-lived technical logs to keep the site secure and working.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we use it, and our lawful basis</h2>
        <p>We use your details to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            email you about Sea Air Club: launch dates, booking access and exclusive opening offers
          </li>
          <li>
            understand which postcards, links and posts bring people to us, so we know what's
            working
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Our lawful basis is your <strong>consent</strong>, which you give when you join (UK GDPR
          Article 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it at any time by using the unsubscribe link in any of
          our emails or by contacting us. We'll never sell your details or share them with anyone
          for their own marketing.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it's stored</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Vercel</strong> hosts this website. Sign-ups are saved in a private storage area
            with Vercel, in its London region.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>ResNexus</strong> is the booking and guest system we use for the cabins. We
            import the early access list into its email marketing tool to send you our emails.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <!-- prettier-ignore -->
        <p>
          Both companies are based in the United States, so your details may be accessed from or
          stored outside the UK. Where that happens, they're protected by
          <span class={tbc} data-tbc>[transfer safeguard to be confirmed]</span>, as UK data
          protection law requires.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep your details until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them. If you unsubscribe,
          we may keep just your email address on a "do not email" list, so we don't contact you
          again by mistake.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under UK data protection law, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you</li>
          <li>have it corrected if it's wrong or incomplete</li>
          <li>have it deleted</li>
          <li>withdraw your consent at any time</li>
          <li>ask us to restrict or stop using it</li>
          <li>receive it in a format you can take elsewhere</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To use any of these rights, contact us using the details below. It's free, and we'll reply
          within one month.
        </p>
        <!-- prettier-ignore -->
        <p>
          If you're unhappy with how we've handled your data, please tell us first so we can put it
          right. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO),
          the UK's data protection regulator, at
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a>
          or on 0303 123 1113.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
        <p>
          We use Vercel Web Analytics to count visits and see which pages are read. It's cookieless:
          it doesn't set cookies, doesn't collect personal data and doesn't identify you. This site
          doesn't use tracking or advertising cookies.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <!-- prettier-ignore -->
        <p>
          For questions about this notice or your data, email
          {site.contactEmail
            ? <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>
            : <span class={tbc} data-tbc>[contact email to be confirmed]</span>}.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
        <p>If anything changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</SimplePage>
